# frozen_string_literal: true

# The demo's bundle, which is the client library's bundle plus a Kafka client.
#
# THE CLIENT'S OWN PINS ARE INHERITED RATHER THAN REPEATED. The demo loads the library from
# ../lib, so it must run it against the `grpc` and `google-protobuf` versions it was built and
# tested against - and a second copy of those pins is a pin that drifts in one of the two places
# without anything noticing. `eval_gemfile` reads the module's Gemfile, groups and all;
# .bundle/config beside this file drops the development and test group, so a demo run installs
# rubocop, rspec and the protoc toolchain not at all.
eval_gemfile "../Gemfile"

# RUBY'S OWN KAFKA CLIENT, for the AK core arm - librdkafka behind an FFI binding, which is what a
# Ruby application actually consumes Kafka with today (it is what Karafka is built on). The
# alternative, the pure-Ruby `ruby-kafka`, was rejected on a fact rather than a preference: it has
# been archived by its authors since 2023, and a comparison whose serial arm is an unmaintained
# gem would flatter the sidecar for a reason that has nothing to do with Parallel Consumer.
#
# It ships precompiled for Linux, so the demo container builds it without a C toolchain; on other
# platforms `bundle install` builds librdkafka from source and needs one. demo/README.md says so.
gem "rdkafka", "0.29.0"
